    },
    "event_ledger": {
        "control_out1_hypothesis": "At h7.5 two aircraft each book one crew; h7.75 one available crew physically and nominally leaves in one positive zero-duration OUT tranche; no transfer backorder. Both prep complete h8, first formation departs h8, completes/returns h9; second wave two parallel preps [19.5,20), departure h20, completion/return h21. Terminal local crew2, free2, booked0, pendingOUT0, completedOUT1, aircraft ready2.",
        "child_out2_hypothesis": "At h7.5 two aircraft each book one crew; h7.75 request2, nominal decreases2, one available crew physically leaves in a positive zero-duration tranche, one transfer backorder remains. At h8 positive second tranche qty1 follows one/both prep releases with exact causal linkage, no double decrement, backorder closes. First formation h8–9. Second wave one remaining local crew forces serial prep [19.5,20) and [20,20.5), departure20.5, completion/return21.5. Terminal local crew1, free1, booked0, pendingOUT0, completedOUT2, aircraft ready2.",
        "task_linkage": "Parse full timed and untimed log, not loose substring matches: request/quantity, backorder snapshots, each created/started/arrived transfer task (including zero-unit diagnostic tasks if any), positive tranche sums, preparation booking/deallocation/wait, aircraft IDs, mission lifecycle, queue/availability and return/ready lines; preserve same-time causal line order. Never assume inherited task IDs; no unknown extra typed event or early cancellation.",
