    "native_and_provenance_gate": {
        "stage_order_each_arm": ["import", "export", "check_import_export", "calc", "jsonreport", "check_behavior"],
        "both_runs": "Use two serial, separately approved native runs in this exact order: control_out1 then child_out2. Each arm requires its own exact frozen manifest/input/run ID/runner/method, actual zero-native SSH5 -PreflightOnly receipt with absent *that arm's* run path, and separate independent GO_PRELAUNCH bound to that arm's exact source map and receipt. The first approval does not authorize the second. After control finishes naturally, first seal its original raw/closure, verify every integer0 capture, valid checker JSON, all 5,210 control cells and complete typed ledger. On any failure preserve NO_GO and do NOT conduct the child's preflight or launch. Only after a control GO may root start a fresh child -PreflightOnly, independent approval, and launch sequence. Before each native dispatch root freshly rechecks GUI identity/responsiveness, WTS, mutex, sshd ancestry, broad runner absence, source hashes and that arm's unique absent run path; control's existing sealed run is expected during child preflight and must not be treated as an absent child. Hold the serial mutex through each natural child completion. Never rerun accepted parent. No stop/kill/timeout/retry.",
        "capture": "Actual PS5 session0/sshd ancestry, sole protected responding GUI13340/session1/start1790590196826/WTS active, broad competing-runner guard, native/checker PID/session/int OS exit/UTC/program/argv, original byte stdout/stderr, source before/after, 23 raw seals per six-step arm if same topology, closure/failure even on NO_GO. Exact counts are confirmed from generated runner schema before approval, never inferred from a synthetic fixture.",
        "converter": {"each_arm_summary_exact": "Input conversion completed. Errors: 0, Warnings: 2, Notes: 0", "ordered_warning_records_exactly_once_each": [{"form": "Control", "record": 1, "code": 108, "line": "rec 1: (warning #108) Enabling simulation log may generate extensive data in log file", "source_reason": "Control.ENLOG=Y"}, {"form": "System", "record": 1, "code": 126, "line": "rec 1: (warning #126) This system contains no items: TEACH-AIR-01", "source_reason": "fixed System TEACH-AIR-01 has no Item rows"}], "matching_rule": "Decode sealed native run.log, permit only native CRLF/LF line-ending representation and separately verified arm-specific Input/Output file paths. Require exact Form: Control then Form: System section ownership, exact rec/code/message lines with anchored whole-line equality and order, exactly one of each, no other warning/error/note record and no source identity mismatch. Require exactly one exact summary line. A warning code seen in unrelated text or wrong form/record does not count.", "stage_gate": "Run the known six stages in order: import→export→check_import_export→calc→jsonreport→check_behavior. Before calc, require only exact source/input/export full32-table type-sensitive roundtrip and roundtrip checker actual integer0 plus valid versioned JSON/typed pass; run.log converter diagnostics do not exist yet. After calc exits actual integer0 and its original run.log is sealed, require the exact two warning records and Errors0/Warnings2/Notes0 summary above as an internal runner gate BEFORE launching jsonreport or accepting behavior. If run.log is missing/uncaptured, warning ownership/text/count differs, SXI/SXO is absent/invalid, or an error/extra note appears, seal NO_GO immediately and do not start jsonreport or check_behavior. No extra native/test stage or retry. Preserve every failure unchanged."},
    },
    "source_lineage": {
